<document
    `{ author: chef }
    <stack
        <heading `{level: 1} "Pancakes">

        <recipe `{serves: 4}
            <ingredient `{amount: "200g"} "flour">
            <ingredient `{amount: "2"} "eggs">
            <ingredient `{amount: "300ml"} "milk">
            <step "Whisk everything into a smooth batter.">
            <step "Fry in a hot, lightly buttered pan.">
        >

        <text "This renderer has no recipe vocabulary, so the recipe, its
               ingredients, and its steps render structurally through the generic
               fallback — labeled, inspectable, intact. A recipe-aware renderer
               would lay the same value out as a card with a checklist. Same
               document, richer reading: nothing was rejected, no schema migration,
               no type discriminators — recognition simply went deeper.">
    >
>
